  "commit_message": "Update EnvironmentValueArrayDecoder to emit empty values when present (#133)\n\n### Motivation\n\nCloses #122\n\n### Modifications\n\n- Set `omittingEmptySubsequences` to `false` in\n`String.split(separator:omittingEmptySubsequences:)` when decoding a\nstring that represents Bool, Int, or Double arrays separated by commas\nin `EnvironmentValuesProvider`.\n- Update `CLIArgumentParser.swift:125` to use `split` instead of\n`components(separatedBy:)`, ensuring homogeneous usage of Swift’s\nsplitting APIs.\n\n### Result\n\nA string representing an array of values separated by `\",\"` will now\nemit empty values when two separators appear together while parsing\n`EnvironmentValuesProvider` dictionaries.\nThis results in treating an empty value as an empty string and,\nconsequently, throwing an error when parsed by individual value decoders\nfor Int, Double, and Bool.\n\nThe additional update enforces homogeneous API usage and favors Swift’s\nnative `split(separator:)` method.\n\n### Test Plan\n\nAdd tests covering empty values in Int, Double, and Bool arrays.",
  "commit_url": "https://github.com/apple/swift-configuration/commit/f7a76a251e32cc905950fcf718cd49bf764327c8",
